<!-- holo — a CANCELLING RACE over the flows its block opens. The first flow to settle yields the
     block's result, and every losing arm cancels RECURSIVELY — the whole subtree beneath a loser,
     never its direct children alone:

         <<~ holo>>
           <<~ lele "lar:///target-a">>
           <<~ lele "lar:///target-b">>
         <<~/holo>>

     `puka` keeps the other discipline: there a loser runs on until the enclosing scope exits.
     `race` mirrors this head in English and delegates here.

     THE PAGE STAYS CLEAR. Coordination governs execution and never layout, so the definition hands
     the compile layer a data annotation naming the discipline and renders nothing. -->

\procedure ~holo()
<span class="lar-holo" data-losers="cancelled-recursively" hidden="true"/>
\end
